XLSX pivot tables keep the file's values caption

Excel names the values field of a pivot table with the definition's
dataCaption, "Values" by default, and shows it in the field's header
cell when two or more values sit on rows or columns. The import
dropped it, so Calc wrote its own "Data" in that cell, and the export
always wrote dataCaption="Values" (Ely R15.11j). The import now names
the data layout field with the file's caption, or "Values" when the
file has none; the export writes the data layout field's name, or
"Values" when it has none. testTdf112106 saves such a file as XLS and
now reads Excel's "Values" back.
diff --git a/sc/qa/unit/pivottable_filters_test.cxx b/sc/qa/unit/pivottable_filters_test.cxx
index 12a3607..12d0f51 100644
--- a/sc/qa/unit/pivottable_filters_test.cxx
+++ b/sc/qa/unit/pivottable_filters_test.cxx
@@ -2243,7 +2243,8 @@ CPPUNIT_TEST_FIXTURE(ScPivotTableFiltersTest, testTdf112106)
     CPPUNIT_ASSERT(pDim);
     const std::optional<OUString>& pLayoutName = pDim->GetLayoutName();
     CPPUNIT_ASSERT(pLayoutName);
-    CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL(ScResId(STR_PIVOT_DATA), (*pLayoutName));
+    // The XLSX file's dataCaption, not Calc's "Data".
+    CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL(u"Values"_ustr, (*pLayoutName));
 }
 
